-- ---- INHERITED, AND RESTATED SO THEY SURVIVE A LANGUAGE ------------
--
-- EIGHTEEN STANDING INVARIANTS BROKE THE MOMENT GERMAN LANDED, and not
-- one of them because anything was wrong. Every one counted ROWS --
-- "exactly one row carries {0}{1}{2}" -- in a world where there was only
-- ever one row per key. A second language doubles the count and the
-- assertion fails while the rule it states is still true of every row.
--
-- That is worth recording as a shape rather than as eighteen edits: an
-- invariant written as a positive count encodes an assumption about how
-- many rows exist, silently, and the first thing that changes the row
-- count exposes it. Twelve of the eighteen are SLOT rules, which is the
-- sharpest version of it -- those exist FOR translators, so the check
-- most needed the day a language arrives is the one guaranteed to break
-- that day.
--
-- Each is retired in place at its own migration, its text kept as `was:`,
-- and restated here counting VIOLATIONS instead of matches. Strictly
-- stronger: `= 0` holds for English, for German, and for every language
-- after them without being edited again.
--
